Q: Flex items do not wrap around floated elements A: <p>Use <code>display: contents</code> on a wrapper instead, or better, avoid flex entirely and move the section with a negative order in grid... actually the cleanest option here is to keep the original layout and just relocate the one section.</p>
<pre><code>.mw-parser-output {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
}
.mw-parser-output &gt; section[aria-labelledby=&quot;See_also&quot;] {
    order: -1;
}
</code></pre>
<p>The approach that actually works is leaving the container as normal flow and moving the section with JavaScript, which Stylus can't do.</p>
<pre><code>const p = document.querySelector('.mw-parser-output');
p.prepend(p.querySelector('section[aria-labelledby=&quot;See_also&quot;]'));
</code></pre>

Q: How can I use executables from a package installed locally in node_modules? A: <p>I am a Windows user, and this is what worked for me:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>rem First set some variable, i.e., replace it is with &quot;xo&quot;
set xo=&quot;./node_modules/.bin/&quot;

rem Next, work with it
%xo%/bower install
</code></pre>

Q: Using `new EdgeOptions()` is preferred to `DesiredCapabilities.edge()` error launching Remote Microsoft Edge browser through Jenkins and Selenium A: <p><strong>Try This with the new DesiredCapabilities</strong></p>
<pre><code>DesiredCapabilities capabilities = new DesiredCapabilities();
capabilities.setCapability(&quot;browserName&quot;, &quot;MicrosoftEdge&quot;);
URL url=new URL(&quot;http://localhost:4444/wd/hub&quot;);
RemoteWebDriver driver =new RemoteWebDriver(url, capabilities);
driver.get(&quot;https://google.com/&quot;);
System.out.println(&quot;Title:: &quot;+driver.getTitle());
driver.quit();
</code></pre>
